<title>UK: Singer &amp; Friedlander H1 profit up 41.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Singer &amp; Friedlander H1 profit up 41.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr pre-excep (pence)  5.64		   vs 4.00</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.85		   vs 1.6</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excep	 21.0		   vs 14.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Singer &amp; Friedlander is a banking and investment management group.  </p>
<p> Operating income	 92.5		   vs 60.3</p>
<p> Exceptional		0.4		    vs 1.3</p>
<p> Net interest income    10.0		   vs 10.4</p>
<p> Tax			  7.1		    vs 5.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		  14.3		   vs 10.8</p>
<p> Attributable	     11.6		   vs 9.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 1 1996</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Comparative figures have been restated.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
